    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">N. of e-justice interventions piloted in Cabo Delgado
N. of community based interventions for justice and law enforcement agencies designed</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">N/A</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Support output 113064-113066 in completing the consultation process for the revision of the law on community courts and the community policing strategy</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- 450 participants from 11 provinces, including community judges, state and non-state actors took part in an initiative led the Ministry of Justice to revise the legal framework establishing community courts.
- 400 representatives of the Police of the Rep of Mozambique and community representatives embarked a holistic policy reform to institutionalize community policing mechanisms.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Pilot e-justice initiatives to expand access to legal aid and protection of HR institutions
- Support community based justice and security initiatives
- Train law enforcement on youth engagement in post-conflict societies</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Recruited a consultant to develop the National Community Policing strategy within the PRM and conducted national consultations processes
- Almost finalized the organization of the first training on youth engagement for the Police in Cabo Delgado Province with a focus on 6 districts affected by the armed conflict</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
